<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; img-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'"><title>Nathan AI · Subject Catalog</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css"><script type="module" src="catalog.mjs"></script></head><body><main>
<header><p class="eyebrow">NATHAN AI · ONE LIBRARY</p><h1>A place for every source.</h1><p>Library of Congress-style subject shelves, original work status, and the B / 8 / inversions finding aid.</p><p class="note">Subject assignments remain provisional. Original words and source identities stay intact.</p></header>
<section aria-label="Collection overview" id="overview" class="overview"></section>
<section class="import"><h2>Open your catalog</h2><p>Select <strong>owner-catalog.json</strong> from the organized archive. Your catalog stays in this browser session.</p><label class="button">Choose catalog<input id="import" type="file" accept=".json,application/json"></label><span id="message" role="status" aria-live="polite">Public view shows subject totals. Import your catalog to browse individual records.</span></section>
<section><h2>Subject shelves</h2><div id="shelves" class="shelves"></div></section>
<section aria-labelledby="finding"><h2 id="finding">Find a source. See what remains.</h2><div class="filters"><label>Search<input id="q" type="search" placeholder="Title, source, shelf ID or match"></label><label>Scope<select id="scope"><option value="b8">B / 8 / inversions</option value="all">Entire imported catalog</option></select></label><label>Subject<select id="class"><option value="">All subjects</option></select></label><label>Source status<select id="status"><option value="">All statuses</option></select></label><label>Review<select id="review"><option value="">All review states</option><option>OPEN</option><option>IN_REVIEW</option><option>REVIEWED</option><option>DEFERRED</option></select></label></div><p id="count" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Title / source</th><th>Subject / match</th><th>Original state / next action</th><th>Your review</th></tr></thead><tbody id="rows"></tbody></table></div><nav aria-label="Result pages"><button id="prev">Previous</button><span id="page"></span><button id="next">Next</button></nav><button id="export" disabled>Export review notes</button><p class="note">Reviewed means the catalog entry was reviewed. Original manuscript or software completion status is preserved separately.</p></section>
<section><h2>Work left to do</h2><div id="tasks"></div></section><footer>Original sources remain owner-controlled. Number, shape, spelling and sound matches retain their separate meanings. <a href="README.md">Method and coverage</a></footer></main></body></html>
